{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From male even to female you shall send out</b> — just as Adam, Eve, and the serpent were banished from the Garden of Eden. And the parashah of the sotah is juxtaposed because the serpent came upon Eve and his thighs fell, as written: \"upon your belly you shall crawl.\" And the parashah of the nazirite is juxtaposed on account of the fruit that the first Adam ate — \"his grapes are grapes of poison.\"" "<b>And they shall not defile</b> — two times: here, and the other: \"and the house of Israel shall no longer defile My holy name\" — that if they defile their camps, they defile the name of My holiness, as written: \"to defile My sanctuary, to profane My holy name.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase מזכר עד נקבה תשלחו does not appear verbatim in Numbers 5:3; the verse reads מזכר עד נקבה תשלחו, and the lemma may reflect Ba'al HaTurim's composite phrasing.", 1 "The two cited phrases combine language from Ezekiel 36:20 and Ezekiel 43:8; Ba'al HaTurim weaves them together in his characteristic compressed manner."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:07.941661237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}